<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ashur-uballit I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1365–1330 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century-bce">14th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ashur-uballit I was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> from 1365 to 1330 BCE. He freed Assyria from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni</a> domination and established it as a great power, corresponding with the Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> as an equal. His reign is regarded as the beginning of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-assyrian-empire">Middle Assyrian</a> kingdom and a foundation of the Assyrian Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ashur-uballit-i.jpg" alt="Ashur-uballit I" width="320" height="326" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gary Todd · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Assyrian_Cuneiform_Script_-_36562326005.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
